Bundled and fetched third-party components
------------------------------------------
The build fetches the following at configure time, each pinned by commit in CMakeLists.txt.
Their licences are reproduced in full by their own repositories; the SPDX identifier is given
here so a distributor can honour the attribution requirement.

  nlohmann/json       9cca280a4d0ccf0c08f47a99aa71d1b0e52f8d03   MIT
  boostorg/pfr        3fe5ce61eee743c6da097c28bc0b84bdf29f6cc4   BSL-1.0
  Neargye/magic_enum  e046b69a3736d314fad813e159b1c192eaef92cd   MIT
  fmtlib/fmt          40626af88bd7df9a5fb80be7b25ac85b122d6c21   MIT
  sammycage/lunasvg   83c58df8103dc7dca423dfd824992af94d49bed6   MIT

The following is vendored rather than fetched, because the build must not need the network:

  ocornut/imgui        1.91.5 (third_party/imgui/)                MIT
  (Dear ImGui, plus its backends/imgui_impl_opengl3 backend; the
   in-game menu is drawn through the game's own GL context)

The following is vendored as a prebuilt static library under lib/ARM64/ and is not rebuilt here:

  GlossHook (libGlossHook.a)                                      MIT

The Android NDK's libc++ is linked dynamically and shipped by the client APK
(libc++_shared.so); it is covered by the LLVM/University of Illinois licence.

